### 13.1 Eliminate feature drift between the React preview and standalone app

The two implementations currently differ in working interactions. For example, the React preview lacks note and event edit actions that exist in the standalone implementation.

Choose one canonical application and ensure that all user-facing functionality remains consistent.

Do not declare success merely because a feature has been added to `daylight/src/app.js` if the React preview is still the interface the user runs.

If the React preview is retained, it must also have functioning forms, dialogs, delete operations, and persistence behavior.

