The React preview header currently points at a v1.1.0 ZIP even though the project contains newer v1.1.2 release artifacts.

Update all visible release links and labels to point at the correct current version.

Use a single documented version source wherever practical. Do not hardcode an outdated version in one location while generating a different version elsewhere.

Verify that every displayed download link actually resolves to the intended artifact.

### 13.4 Keep the release build trustworthy

Retain the standalone esbuild bundling process and classic-script syntax validation.

Update the build as needed so the generated release includes all current functionality.

Never overwrite historical release archives during ordinary builds.

Use an explicit new release version after inspecting existing versions. Version 1.2.0 is the intended next target for this feature set if no later release already exists.

